 "boundary": "Every remaining CIP label and SMARTS cell has a named root cause; none is unclassified. The 6 CIP labels are 4 phosphorus centres CheMatic abstains on as oracle_unstable, 1 trivalent bridgehead nitrogen CheMatic does not model, and 1 centre (row 4480, atom 3) where both engines label and disagree and which needs independent adjudication before either answer is adopted. The 200 SMARTS cells are ring-count semantics: [Rn]/[kn] count SSSR rings in CheMatic and RDKit's symmetrized ring set in RDKit (194 cells), plus 6 cells on a ferrocene row. This is not a claim of complete RDKit CIP or SMARTS compatibility."
